set_option linter.unusedVariables false

/-!
# A308505

Counterclockwise square spiral of distinct positive integers constructed by greedy algorithm, such that for p = 2 and 3, every multiple of p (except p itself) is vertically or horizontally adjacent to a cell already holding a multiple of p.

The 67 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A308505

/-- Known terms of `A308505`, starting at index `1`. -/
def data : List retType :=
  [1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 4, 8,
    10, 6, 9, 15, 19, 23, 25, 29, 31, 35,
    37, 41, 43, 14, 16, 20, 22, 26, 12, 18,
    21, 27, 33, 39, 45, 47, 49, 53, 55, 59,
